<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nikol Pashinyan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1975">1975</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nikol Pashinyan is an Armenian journalist and politician who led the peaceful protests of 2018, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/velvet-revolution">Velvet Revolution</a>, which brought him to power as prime minister. His government faced defeat in the 2020 war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagorno-karabakh">Nagorno-Karabakh</a> and the loss of the region in 2023, which drove out over 100,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a> and cooled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>'s relations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nikol-pashinyan.jpg" alt="Nikol Pashinyan" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stenbocki maja · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:K%C3%A4tlemine_Armeenia_peaminister_Pashinyan%27iga_(552477480461).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The crisis of the system came in 2018, when Serzh Sargsyan's third consecutive term provoked protests led by the parliamentarian <b>Nikol Pashinyan</b> of Civil Contract; Sargsyan resigned, parliament elected Armen Sarkissian president in March and Pashinyan prime minister in May.</blockquote><a href="/empire/armenia">Armenia · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>On 8 August 2025 President Ilham Aliyev and the Armenian prime minister <b>Nikol Pashinyan</b> signed a joint declaration at the White House committing to a peace deal, facilitated by the Trump administration, to end nearly four decades of conflict.</blockquote><a href="/empire/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan · Into the Present</a></li></ul></section>
